"""Manually reviewed image-dependent questions. No filename-based answer generation."""
import random
Q=[]
def q(n,stem,choices,clue,wrong,concept=None,visual_clues=None,**kw):
 """Pass source_id, variant_id, collection, question_type or format_version through kw. Options are shuffled deterministically by n so the correct answer is not always first."""
 options=choices.split('|');rat=[clue]+wrong.split('|');assert len(options)==len(rat) and len(options) in (4,5),(n,options,rat)
 order=list(range(len(options)));random.Random(n).shuffle(order)
 Q.append(dict(n=n,stem=stem,options=[options[i] for i in order],correct_index=order.index(0),explanation=clue,choice_rationales=[rat[i] for i in order],visual_clues=visual_clues or [clue],tested_concept=concept or options[0],**kw))
q(5,'Which developmental stage is shown in the complete micrograph?','Blastocyst|Morula|Single-cell zygote|Bilaminar embryonic disc','A large cavity is enclosed by a thin cellular rim, with a compact inner cell mass at one pole.','A solid ball of cells would not have this dominant internal cavity.|The image has many cells and a cavity, not one undivided cell.|Two flat embryonic cell layers are not the dominant structure shown.')
q(8,'Which description best fits the central breast lesion on this ultrasound?','Anechoic cyst with posterior enhancement|Solid mass with posterior shadowing|Complex cyst with a mural nodule|Irregular mass with spiculated margins','The oval lesion has a black interior, a smooth border, and brighter tissue deep to it.','The interior is anechoic and the tissue behind it is bright, not shadowed.|No solid mural projection interrupts the black cavity.|The contour is smooth and oval rather than irregular or spiculated.')
q(9,'What architectural change occupies the breast duct in this field?','Intraluminal epithelial proliferation|Isolated single cells infiltrating stroma|Necrosis replacing adipocytes|Widely spaced normal double-layered ducts','Crowded epithelial cells bridge and partially fill one expanded ductal lumen.','The cells remain clustered inside the duct rather than forming isolated stromal files.|The central structure is an epithelial duct, not injured fat.|The many intraluminal cell layers exceed a normal thin duct lining.')
q(10,'Which tissue reaction is most evident in this breast micrograph?','Inflammation around disrupted fat spaces|Cribriform epithelial growth inside a duct|Single-file stromal infiltration|Papillary fronds inside a cyst','Numerous empty fat spaces are surrounded by cellular inflammatory and fibrous tissue.','There is no epithelial duct filled by rounded punched-out spaces.|Linear rows of infiltrating epithelial cells are not shown.|There are no branching epithelial-covered fibrovascular cores.')
q(11,'Which arrangement best describes the ovarian tumor in this field?','Rounded epithelial nests in fibrous stroma|Thyroid follicles filled with colloid|Small follicles around eosinophilic droplets|Glomeruloid bodies around central vessels','Broad rounded nests of pale epithelial cells sit in dense, pink fibrous stroma.','The nests are solid rather than colloid-filled thyroid follicles.|The dominant units are broad solid nests, not tiny spaces around pink droplets.|No central vessel suspended within a tumor-lined space is shown.')
q(12,'Which nuclear feature is visible in these ovarian tumor cells?','Longitudinal nuclear grooves|Eosinophilic intranuclear inclusions|Multinuclear molding|Peripheral displacement by large mucin vacuoles','Several oval nuclei have longitudinal clefts, producing a coffee-bean appearance.','The clefts are linear grooves rather than round pink nuclear inclusions.|The image shows separate nuclei rather than molded nuclei crowded in one giant cell.|Large mucin vacuoles pushing nuclei to the cell edge are absent.')
q(18,'Which epithelial transition is present across this cervical section?','Stratified squamous to columnar epithelium|Urothelium to keratinized squamous epithelium|Simple squamous to cuboidal epithelium|Respiratory epithelium to intestinal epithelium','The multilayered squamous surface on the left meets tall columnar cells on the right.','Neither umbrella-cell urothelium nor a keratinized surface is demonstrated.|The left side is multilayered, not a single flat lining.|The right surface lacks an intestinal crypt pattern and the left is squamous.')
q(24,'Which cytopathic feature is most conspicuous in the squamous epithelium?','Koilocytosis|Multinuclear molding|Intranuclear eosinophilic inclusions|Full-thickness loss of squamous maturation','Upper epithelial cells have sharply defined perinuclear clear halos with enlarged dark nuclei.','The dominant change is a halo around individual nuclei, not tightly molded giant-cell nuclei.|Round pink inclusions within nuclei are not the prominent finding.|The epithelium still shows maturation toward the surface.')
q(26,'Where are the dense deposits indicated by the two large arrows on this head CT?','Along the ventricular margins|Within the skull bones only|Within an extra-axial crescent|Confined to the cortical sulci','The bright deposits follow the margins of the enlarged lateral ventricles.','The arrows end deep to the skull on ventricular margins.|The deposits are central and periventricular, not a peripheral crescent.|The large arrows point to ventricular walls rather than cortical sulci.','Periventricular calcification')
q(28,'What visible dental morphology affects the upper central incisors?','Notched incisal edges|Multiple extra incisors|Complete absence of incisors|Diffuse gingival overgrowth','Both upper central incisors have a central indentation along their biting edges.','The striking finding is the shape of the existing incisors, not extra teeth.|The incisors are present and visible.|The abnormality is in the tooth edges rather than enlarged gingiva.','Hutchinson-type notched incisors')
q(33,'Which growth pattern is shown within the expanded breast ducts?','Cribriform pattern|Single-file pattern|Papillary pattern with fibrovascular cores|Spindle-cell fascicular pattern','Rounded punched-out spaces perforate crowded epithelial proliferations within ducts.','Cells are packed into ductal groups rather than thin stromal files.|The small spaces lack branching fibrovascular stalks.|The lesion is epithelial and rounded, not composed of spindle-cell bundles.')
q(34,'What occupies the center of the large involved breast duct?','Necrotic debris|Mature adipose tissue|A fibrovascular stalk|A colloid-filled thyroid follicle','The duct center contains granular dark debris surrounded by a rim of tumor cells.','The central material is granular rather than clear fat vacuoles.|No vascular connective-tissue core supports the central material.|There is no smooth colloid pool enclosed by a thyroid follicular lining.','Comedo-type central necrosis')
q(35,'Which gross finding most strongly identifies the nature of this opened ovarian cyst?','Hair and sebaceous material|Smooth empty cavity without contents|Uniform solid white cut surface|Translucent grape-like vesicles','Visible hair strands and greasy material occupy the cyst, supporting a mature cystic teratoma.','The cavity contains abundant hair and material.|The lesion is a cavity with contents rather than a solid white mass.|The specimen is one opened hair-containing cyst, not a cluster of translucent vesicles.','Mature cystic teratoma')
q(38,'Which paired cell populations characterize this ovarian tumor field?','Large pale cells with small dark lymphocytes|Spindle cells with mature adipocytes|Mucin-laden signet-ring cells with fibroblasts|Thyroid follicular cells surrounding colloid','Large pale tumor cells with conspicuous nuclei are interspersed with much smaller dark lymphocytes.','The tumor cells are rounded and pale, not spindle shaped, and mature fat is absent.|Large mucin vacuoles displacing nuclei to the edge are not shown.|The field lacks colloid-filled follicles.','Dysgerminoma cell morphology')
q(680,'Which labeled interval shows a testosterone peak while sperm production remains at baseline?','Interval a|Interval b|Interval c|Interval d','Interval a contains the fetal testosterone peak without a corresponding rise in the blue sperm-production curve.','Interval b is the low childhood interval.|Both curves rise through interval c.|Both curves are high in interval d.','Fetal testosterone without spermatogenesis')
q(746,'How does estrogen excretion change after the point marked menopause on this graph?','Declines toward a low plateau|Continues with large cyclic peaks|Rises steadily to its lifetime maximum|Falls immediately to zero','The red curve falls after menopause and then levels off above zero.','Large repeated peaks occur before menopause.|The postmenopausal segment slopes downward.|The final segment remains above the zero baseline.','Postmenopausal estrogen trajectory')
q(775,'Which curve peaks in the first trimester and then falls to a lower plateau?','Human chorionic gonadotropin|Progesterone|Estrogens|All three curves','The red hCG curve peaks near weeks 10 to 12 and falls while the other two rise later.','The black progesterone curve rises through much of pregnancy.|The blue estrogen curve rises markedly in later pregnancy.|Only the red curve has the large early peak.','Pregnancy hormone timing')
q(827,'Between which adjacent stages does the plotted pulmonary vascular resistance fall most sharply?','Fetus to newborn|Newborn to infant|Infant to adult|Resistance rises at every transition','The first segment has the largest downward slope, from about 200 to about 60 arbitrary units.','This segment falls only modestly compared with the first.|The final segment has a smaller decline.|Every plotted segment slopes downward.','Pulmonary vascular resistance at birth')
q(593,'Compare both panels. Which relationship between the growth spurt and gonadal development is plotted?','Female peak height velocity occurs earlier in age than the male peak|Male peak height velocity occurs earlier in age than the female peak|The two peaks occur at the same age|Both peaks occur before gonadal development begins','The female height-spurt curve peaks around age 12, while the male curve peaks around age 14.','The male peak sits farther right on its age axis.|The maxima occupy different ages.|The gonadal-development bars begin before the curve maxima.','Sex comparison of pubertal growth spurts',panels='joint')
q(655,'Using both panels, which pair of plotted ranges has the earliest left boundary for its sex?','Breast budding in girls and growth of scrotum/testes in boys|Menarche in girls and growth spurt in boys|Adult breast size in girls and facial hair in boys|Underarm hair in girls and body-shape change in boys','The breast-budding range begins at the left edge of the girls panel, while scrotal/testicular growth begins among the earliest ranges in the boys panel.','Both selected ranges begin later than the earliest bars.|These bars begin well after the earliest changes.|These ranges also start later on their respective axes.','Sequence of pubertal event ranges',panels='joint')
q(635,'What station corresponds to the head contour whose presenting point lies on the red line connecting the ischial spines?','0 station|Minus 3 station|Plus 3 station|Plus 5 station','The red line joining the ischial spines defines zero; the contour at that line is station 0.','Minus 3 lies above the line.|Plus 3 lies below the line.|Plus 5 is near the outlet, well below the line.','Fetal station at the ischial spines')
q(713,'Where is the positive brown immunostaining located in this field?','Predominantly in nuclei|Exclusively along cell membranes|Only in extracellular stroma|Only inside glandular lumina','Brown staining occupies rounded nuclear profiles among blue unstained nuclei.','There are no continuous brown rings outlining cell membranes.|The brown signal is concentrated in cells rather than stromal matrix.|The signal is not confined to empty glandular spaces.','Nuclear immunostaining localization')
q(709,'According to this supplied chart, how does the rate with both exposures compare with the rate with neither exposure?','More than thirtyfold higher|Approximately equal|Approximately fivefold higher|Lower','The displayed rates are 28.5 and 0.8 per 10,000 person-years, giving a ratio of 35.63. This is interpretation of the supplied figure, not a current risk estimate.','The bars differ greatly in height.|A fivefold increase would be much smaller than the ratio shown.|The combined-exposure bar is the tallest.','Interpreting the supplied DVT rate chart')
q(268,'Which organism form crosses the squamous cells in this smear?','Branching fungal pseudohyphae|A carpet of coccobacilli obscuring cell borders|Pear-shaped flagellated protozoa|Intracellular viral nuclear inclusions','Long branching filamentous forms cross and entangle squamous cells, the pseudohyphal pattern described for Candida in the lecture.','The prominent structures are long filaments rather than a bacterial coating.|No discrete pear-shaped organisms with axostyles are the dominant finding.|The structures extend across the field outside nuclei.','Candida pseudohyphae')
q(294,'Which combination of nuclear changes is most evident in the large blue cells?','Multinucleation with nuclear molding|Perinuclear halos around isolated nuclei|Peripheral nuclei displaced by mucin|Longitudinal grooves in isolated nuclei','Multiple enlarged nuclei crowd together and mold against one another in individual cells.','The dominant change is crowded multinucleation rather than a halo around one nucleus.|Large cytoplasmic mucin vacuoles are absent.|The nuclei crowd and mold rather than showing isolated longitudinal clefts.','Herpetic multinucleation and molding')
q(338,'Which pattern in this vulvar biopsy best supports lichen sclerosus?','Pale superficial dermal sclerosis beneath thinned epithelium|Marked acanthosis with long rete ridges|Papillary squamous fronds with koilocytes|Invasive keratinizing nests','A broad pale sclerotic band lies beneath a relatively thin surface epithelium, with inflammation deeper in the dermis.','The epidermis is relatively thin rather than markedly acanthotic.|Exophytic papillary fronds are absent.|No infiltrating nests with keratin pearls are shown.','Lichen sclerosus morphology')
q(356,'In this section of uterine muscle, which finding supports adenomyosis?','Endometrial glands and stroma embedded in myometrium|Only interlacing smooth-muscle fascicles|Malignant squamous nests with keratin pearls|Chorionic villi inside a blood-filled space','Islands of endometrial-type glands and dark stroma interrupt the surrounding pink smooth-muscle bundles.','Glandular and stromal islands are clearly present within the muscle.|The islands are glands with stroma, not keratinizing squamous nests.|No villous branching structures are shown.','Adenomyosis morphology')
q(405,'Which named structure is visible in this ovarian tumor field?','Call-Exner bodies|Schiller-Duval bodies|Psammoma bodies|Keratin pearls','Small rosettelike groups of cells enclose rounded pink material, producing Call-Exner bodies.','There is no central vessel within a tumor-lined glomeruloid space.|The bodies are pink microfollicular spaces rather than concentric calcific spherules.|There are no concentric layers of squamous keratin.','Call-Exner bodies')
q(428,'Which tumor-cell morphology is prominent in this field?','Signet-ring cells|Spindle cells in fascicles|Squamous cells forming keratin pearls|Cells forming colloid-filled follicles','Large pale cytoplasmic vacuoles displace nuclei toward the cell edges, producing signet-ring forms.','The cells are rounded and vacuolated rather than elongated bundles.|Concentric keratin pearls are absent.|The pale spaces are intracellular rather than extracellular follicular colloid.','Signet-ring morphology')
q(500,'What are the brightly eosinophilic rodlike structures in the cytoplasm?','Reinke crystals|Psammoma bodies|Call-Exner bodies|Schiller-Duval bodies','Bright red, angular rods lie within the cytoplasm of these Leydig-type cells.','Psammoma bodies are rounded laminated deposits, not intracellular rods.|Call-Exner bodies are multicellular microfollicular arrangements.|Schiller-Duval bodies are vascular glomeruloid structures.','Reinke crystals')
q(550,'Which architectural structure is present at the center of this field?','Schiller-Duval body|Call-Exner body|Psammoma body|Keratin pearl','A central vessel containing red cells is surrounded by tumor within a larger space, creating a glomeruloid Schiller-Duval body.','The central core contains a blood vessel rather than pink microfollicular secretion.|There is no concentric laminated calcific sphere.|There are no concentric squamous keratin layers.','Schiller-Duval body')
q(862,'Which follicular change is evident in this ovarian section?','Atresia with folded glassy membranes|Large intact fluid-filled antrum|Sheets of large luteinized cells|Colloid-filled thyroid follicles','Irregular collapsed follicular outlines contain thick folded pink glassy membranes, matching atretic follicles.','The structures are collapsed rather than dominated by a large intact antrum.|Large pale luteinized cell sheets are not the dominant pattern.|The folded membranes are not smooth colloid-filled thyroid follicles.','Atretic follicles')
q(254,'Which layer is retained when the drawn endometrium sheds during menstruation?','Basal layer|Entire functional layer|Both layers are lost completely|Neither layer changes','The basal band remains continuous while the tall functional layer breaks down at the menstrual intervals.','The functional layer visibly thins and sheds.|The basal band remains in the drawing.|The upper contour changes substantially across the cycle.','Endometrial layer preservation')
q(740,'Which lifespan interval contains the prolonged lowest gonadotropin activity in this schematic?','Childhood|Gestation|Adult reproductive period|Senescence','The red line is lowest over the extended childhood interval, between the infant peak and pubertal rise.','Gestation includes a large early peak.|The adult female curve has repeated peaks.|Both senescent curves rise above their preceding baselines.','Childhood gonadotropin quiescence')
q(841,'Compare panels D and E. How does ureteral duplication differ in the kidney on the image right of each panel?','D has two separate distal ureters; E has distal fusion|D has distal fusion; E has two separate distal ureters|Both show one ureter from the kidney onward|Both show complete separation to the bladder','The duplicated ureters in D remain separate to the bladder, whereas those in E join into a single distal segment.','The visible connections show the reverse relationship.|Two upper ureteral channels are visible on the affected side.|E clearly shows a Y-shaped junction before the bladder.','Complete versus partial ureteral duplication',panels='joint')
q(853,'Which congenital renal configuration is demonstrated by the complete specimen?','Horseshoe kidney|Two completely separate kidneys|Unilateral renal agenesis|Duplicated bladder','The two renal masses are joined across the midline by a broad inferior bridge.','An isthmus visibly connects the two sides.|Two renal masses are present.|The specimen shows renal tissue rather than two bladders.','Horseshoe kidney')
q(579,'Which level is crossed out in this hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis diagram?','Hypothalamic level|Anterior pituitary level|Gonadal level|Peripheral sex-hormone level','The red cross lies over the hypothalamic brain image, upstream of the GnRH arrow.','The pituitary is below the crossed region.|The gonads at the bottom are uncrossed.|The hormone labels below the gonads are uncrossed.','Central HPG axis impairment')
q(584,'Which level is crossed out in this hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis diagram?','Gonadal level|Hypothalamic level|Anterior pituitary level|GnRH secretion arrow','The red cross is centered on the testes and ovaries, downstream of the LH/FSH arrow.','The brain at the top is uncrossed.|The pituitary image is uncrossed.|The GnRH arrow is high above the crossed region.','Primary gonadal HPG axis impairment')
q(962,'Which cell type forms the flattened outer layer surrounding the illustrated secretory epithelium?','Myoepithelial cells|Milk-secreting luminal cells|Adipocytes|Vascular endothelial cells','Flattened elongated cells wrap around the outside of the cuboidal secretory epithelial ring, the position of myoepithelial cells in the supplied lecture.','The luminal cells are the taller inner ring bordering the blue cavity.|The illustrated outer cells are elongated, not large lipid-filled adipocytes.|They surround the secretory unit rather than lining a blood vessel.','Mammary myoepithelial layer')
q(963,'What sonographic appearance do the two yellow arrows identify within this ovary?','Rounded anechoic spaces|Dense calcific foci with acoustic shadows|Uniformly solid echogenic nodules|Irregular infiltrating tissue replacing the ovary','Both arrows point to dark rounded fluid spaces within ovarian tissue, consistent with follicles.','The targets are dark spaces without bright calcific foci or posterior shadows.|Their interiors are anechoic rather than uniformly solid and bright.|The ovarian outline remains visible around discrete rounded spaces.','Ovarian follicle ultrasound appearance')
